{"name":"Red Coral","hex":"#ff4040","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red coral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the species Corallium rubrum of coral, of the Mediterranean Sea, commonly used as an ornament or gem."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_coral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Precious coral","blocks":[{"text":"Precious coral, or red coral, is the common name given to a genus of marine corals, Corallium. The distinguishing characteristic of precious corals is their durable and intensely colored red or pink-orange skeleton, which is used for making jewelry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Corallium_rubrum_%28Linnaeus%2C_1758%29_11.jpg/330px-Corallium_rubrum_%28Linnaeus%2C_1758%29_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Precious_coral"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and secrete calcium carbonate to form a hard skeleton."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg/330px-Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"},{"title":"Coral (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The various tones of the color coral are orange, red and pink representations of the colors of those cnidarians known as precious corals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Parure_realizzata_per_la_regina_Farida_d%27Egitto_%281934%29.JPG/500px-Parure_realizzata_per_la_regina_Farida_d%27Egitto_%281934%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Parure_realizzata_per_la_regina_Farida_d%27Egitto_%281934%29.JPG/500px-Parure_realizzata_per_la_regina_Farida_d%27Egitto_%281934%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Queen Farida of Egypt red coral parure by Ascione, made in 1938 in Naples, Coral Jewellery Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParure_realizzata_per_la_regina_Farida_d'Egitto_(1934).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg/500px-Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg/1280px-Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg/500px-Coral_woman_p1070258.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese coral sculpture","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoral_woman_p1070258.jpg"},{